---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import CookieBanner from '../components/CookieBanner.astro'

// What this page says must match what the site does. If the contact form's
// route (netlify/functions/contact.js), the analytics (components/Analytics.astro)
// or the hosting change, update this page and the French one
// (fr/politique-de-confidentialite.astro) together.
//
// No structured data: this page is marked noindex, like the terms pages.
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  route="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy | Billy Nightingale"
  description="How billynightingale.com handles personal data: the contact form, audience measurement after consent, and your rights."
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <Header lang="en" route="privacy" />
  <main id="legal_main">
    <CookieBanner lang="en" />
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Billy Nightingale – Website Creation &amp; Web Development</strong>
    </p>
    <p>Last updated: 25 November 2026</p>

    <section id="controller">
      <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by Billy Nightingale, a sole trader
        (micro-entrepreneur) based in Capbreton, France. I am the data
        controller for the personal data collected through it.
      </p>
      <p>
        For any question about your data, write to
        <a href="mailto:contact@billynightingale.com">contact@billynightingale.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact-form">
      <h2>2. The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        When you send the contact form, I receive what you entered: your name,
        your email address, the reason for your message and the message
        itself, and, if you filled them in, your business name, your current
        website, and your budget and timeline.
      </p>
      <p>
        I use this only to reply to you and, if you ask for one, to prepare a
        quotation. The legal basis is the steps taken at your request before a
        contract, and my legitimate interest in answering the people who
        contact me.
      </p>
      <p>I do not sell your data, and I do not use it to send newsletters.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="audience">
      <h2>3. Audience measurement</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose “Accept” in the cookie banner, this site loads two
        audience measurement tools: Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity.
        They record how the site is used (pages viewed, clicks, scrolling,
        approximate location, type of device) and place cookies in your
        browser. The legal basis is your consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose “Deny”, or make no choice, neither tool is loaded and
        no audience measurement cookie is placed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your choice is kept in your browser’s local storage, on your device.
        To change it, clear this site’s data in your browser settings: the
        banner will be shown again on your next visit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="recipients">
      <h2>4. Who receives your data</h2>
      <p>
        Your data is handled by me and by the service providers this site
        relies on, each only for the task described:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Netlify</strong> (United States) hosts the website and
          receives the contact form.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (United States) delivers the website and
          protects it against abuse. Like any web server, it processes the IP
          address of each visitor.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Make</strong> (Czech Republic) passes the contact form’s
          message on to me.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Brevo</strong> (France) sends me the message by email if the
          usual route fails, so that your enquiry is not lost.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zoho</strong> (data centre in the European Union) hosts my
          mailbox.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong> and <strong>Microsoft</strong> (United
          States) provide the audience measurement tools, only if you have
          accepted them.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some of these providers are established outside the European Union.
        Transfers to the United States are covered by the EU–US Data Privacy
        Framework or by the European Commission’s standard contractual
        clauses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="retention">
      <h2>5. How long your data is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Messages sent through the contact form are kept for as long as the
        exchange lasts, and for no more than three years after our last
        contact if you do not become a client. If you become a client, the
        documents required by law (quotations, invoices) are kept for the
        legal period.
      </p>
      <p>
        Audience measurement data is kept for the period set by each tool, up
        to 14 months.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="rights">
      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you can ask to
        see the data I hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, limit or
        object to its use, and receive it in a reusable format. You can
        withdraw your consent to audience measurement at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        To use these rights, write to
        <a href="mailto:contact@billynightingale.com">contact@billynightingale.com</a>.
        I will reply within one month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you believe your rights are not respected, you can lodge a
        complaint with the French data protection authority, the CNIL
        (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" rel="noopener">www.cnil.fr</a>).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This page is updated when the website changes how it handles data. The
        date at the top shows the latest version.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
